        {
            "_id": "P7evyX7KwQsp0geh",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp",
            "name": "Parasitic Possession",
            "sort": 400000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The umbral shepherd attempts to possess an adjacent corporeal creature. This has the same effect as the possession spell (DC 22) with an unlimited duration, except they aren't @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Unconscious] and aren't @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Paralyzed] when the effect ends, though they are killed if host dies. A creature possessed by an umbral shepherd applies shadowy sublimation to all its Strikes and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Doomed]{Doomed 1}. This doomed condition doesn't reduce naturally unless the umbral shepherd spends an entire day without possessing the creature. For each consecutive month the shepherd possesses the creature, the doomed value increases by 1, to a maximum of 4.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
